as how are they different I’d see them as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:28.160
two points on a continuum because there's a&nbsp;
lot of overlap in any good kind of pitch but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:39.680
clearly you're talking about one very specific&nbsp;
type of product in Hollywood versus an infinite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:47.520
set of things that you can pitch. The basic&nbsp;
ideas are always going to be the same right that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:59.280
there are a number of factors, again I&nbsp;
keep wanting to move us into persuasion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.360
because I love talking about persuasion, the&nbsp;
psychology of persuasion is an incredible area&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.480
and we know a lot now about how people make&nbsp;
decisions that we didn't know a while ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.280
One of the interesting things for example have you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.840
heard of a book called Thinking&nbsp;
Fast and Slow, Daniel Kahneman?

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.240
Film Courage: I haven't read it but I've seen it.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:35.920
